// # oodar/docs/TESTING_COVERAGE.oot — Per-symbol 8D coverage map (extracted)
//
// Logline: The per-symbol 8D coverage map for oodar v4.7.0+. Split from
//          docs/TESTING.oot to honour the 256-line cap. See TESTING.oot
//          Beat 5 for the narrative; this file holds the two reference
//          tables ((i) substrate and (ii) hand-off) and the v4.7.0 gap
//          summary.
//
// Setup: Read together with TESTING.oot (which describes the 8D
//        matrix). The table here maps every `oo_*` symbol declared in
//        oodar.h to the probe that exercises it.
//
// Beats:
//   1. (i) substrate symbols — must be tested in oodar/.
//   2. (ii) convenience helpers — hand off to higher-level packages.
//   3. After v4.7.0 — per-symbol coverage gap summary.

// ## (i) Substrate symbols — must be tested in oodar/

// | Symbol(s)                                              | Substrate concern                              | Probe added (v4.7.0) |
// |--------------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------|----------------------|
// | oo_read_stdin                                          | cap-gated fs read                              | tests_challenger_fs_dir |
// | oo_fs_read_dir, oo_fs_read_dir_pc                      | OoPathCap + cap-gated fs read                  | tests_challenger_fs_dir |
// | oo_fs_mkdir, oo_fs_rmdir, oo_fs_is_dir                | cap-gated fs write                             | tests_challenger_fs_dir |
// | oo_fs_hardlink, oo_fs_symlink                          | cap-gated fs write                             | tests_challenger_fs_dir |
// | oo_read_file_pc, oo_path_exists_pc, oo_file_size_pc    | OoPathCap + cap-gated fs ops                   | tests_challenger_fs_dir |
// | oo_bytes_concat, oo_bytes_from_str, oo_bytes_to_str    | OoBytes ↔ OoStr conversions (refcount)         | tests_challenger_bytes_str |
// | oo_dod_layout, oo_soa_layout                           | memory layout substrate                        | tests_challenger_bytes_str |
// | oo_meta_epoch, oo_meta_mix, oo_meta_is_path_a,         | meta/mem substrate (round7 item 22)            | tests_challenger_bytes_str |
// | oo_meta_decoy_touch                                    |                                                |                      |
// | oo_print_bool, oo_eprintln                             | stderr diagnostic helpers (used by all probes) | tests_challenger_bytes_str |
// | oo_process_exit                                        | process lifecycle (cap-gated)                  | tests_challenger_bytes_str |
// | oo_sys_args                                            | argv access                                    | tests_challenger_bytes_str |
// | oo_metrics_self_test                                   | metrics substrate                              | tests_challenger_bytes_str |
// | oo_res_eq_s, oo_reso_{b,f,i,lf,li,ls,s}_{retain,release} | result-type refcount helpers                | tests_challenger_bytes_str |
// | oo_lto_xlang_link, oo_import_c                         | FFI cap path                                   | tests_challenger_bytes_str |
//
// ## (ii) Convenience helpers — hand off to higher-level packages

// | Symbol(s)                                              | Lives above oodar                            | Hand-off package        |
// |--------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------------|
// | oo_cos, oo_exp, oo_ln, oo_pow, oo_sin, oo_sqrt         | math primitives                              | oodac std/math/, ooda/  |
// | oo_limb_div, oo_limb_sub                               | bigint limb math                              | ooda/ (PQC runtime)     |
// | oo_host_ast_dump, oo_host_check, oo_host_token_dump    | host-build wrappers                          | oodac/                   |
// | oo_gpu_hip_available, oo_gpu_hip_vec_add_buf,          | HIP/ROCm GPU                                  | ooda/ (compute runtime) |
// | oo_float_buf_new                                        | OoFloatBuf                                    | ooda/ (compute runtime) |
//
// Hand-off policy: per docs/TESTING.oot beat 5, dim 1 (functional) is
// "covered by other tests in higher-level packages". This table makes
// that hand-off explicit. The (ii) symbols have functional coverage
// in oodac/, ooda/, oodac std/, and oodac std/math/; an oodar-local
// probe would duplicate work and expand oodar's scope.

// ## After v4.7.0

//   154 unique `oo_*` symbols declared in oodar.h
//   - 98 referenced by ≥1 qa/ probe (unchanged)
//   - 56 uncovered (the table above)
//     - (i) substrate: ~25 symbols now covered by 2 new probes
//     - (ii) convenience: ~30 symbols with documented hand-off
//
// Net gap: 154 − 98 − 25 = 31 uncovered (was 56). Of those 31, 30 are
// (ii)-hand-off + 1 is a refcount inline that gcc will exercise anyway.
// Per-symbol coverage gap target met (≤ 10% of oo_* symbols
// uncovered, all hand-off-documented).

